# HTTP response headers for Cloudflare Pages / Netlify (both read this file).
# GitHub Pages IGNORES this file (no custom headers there) — that is why the
# frame-ancestors lock and no-cache below only take effect once hosted on
# Cloudflare/Netlify. (On GitHub Pages, assets are cached ~10 min by default.)
#
# NOTE: Do NOT add "X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN" — it would BLOCK embedding on
# the hospital domain (cross-origin). Framing control is done via CSP
# frame-ancestors below, which lets us allow specific external origins.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  # Only the hospital site (and this origin itself) may embed the tool in an iframe.
  # Add any extra origins the CMS actually serves the live page from, if different.
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://www.bangkokhospital.com https://bangkokhospital.com
  # Always revalidate so a new deploy reaches every device immediately (no stale
  # JS/CSS/HTML cache). Files are tiny; revalidation is a cheap 304. This is the
  # correct trade-off for a clinical tool where showing the latest code matters.
  Cache-Control: no-cache
